1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,400
You know, when we talk about the ancestors who came before us and those whose lives were taken,

2
00:00:07,400 --> 00:00:18,260
so often folks are speaking of their ancestral wisdom in terms of the knowledge that they had.

3
00:00:19,120 --> 00:00:26,220
But the wisdom that we can also gain is from the naivete that they had.

4
00:00:26,220 --> 00:00:37,080
Now, as I watch a black man escort this racist fool who stopped through Minnesota and got his nuts handed to him,

5
00:00:38,140 --> 00:00:41,560
I say to myself, have we not learned yet?

6
00:00:41,740 --> 00:00:47,740
Did we not learn from Martin Luther King Jr.'s regretting integrating his people into the burning house?

7
00:00:47,840 --> 00:00:51,900
Did we not learn that there is no moral suasion?

8
00:00:51,900 --> 00:00:59,060
Did we not learn when Stokely Carmichael said, in order to fight an enemy with nonviolence, they have to have a conscience?

9
00:00:59,960 --> 00:01:07,580
Did we not learn when the late Assata Shakur said, nobody in the world, nobody in history has ever gotten their freedom

10
00:01:07,580 --> 00:01:12,080
by appealing to the moral code of those oppressing them?

11
00:01:12,080 --> 00:01:15,320
I want to set y'all free.

12
00:01:18,110 --> 00:01:32,810
Your goodness, your kindness is not measured by how much you put yourself in danger to protect those who would see you slain.

13
00:01:32,810 --> 00:01:46,700
We don't need more martyrs, and we also don't need more folks allowing for the oppressor to think that we are here to protect them.

14
00:01:46,920 --> 00:01:50,760
The great Patrice Lumumba was assassinated on this day in 1960,

15
00:01:50,760 --> 00:01:56,180
and he genuinely believed that there would be freedom for the people of the Democratic Republic of Congo

16
00:01:56,180 --> 00:02:01,260
because he believed that the oppressors that they were negotiating with

17
00:02:01,260 --> 00:02:06,060
were operating under a human code of consciousness and conduct.

18
00:02:07,200 --> 00:02:12,500
You know, the rub is, it's not that they didn't see us as human.

19
00:02:13,460 --> 00:02:15,880
It's that they don't see themselves as human.

20
00:02:15,880 --> 00:02:21,480
So just know that we will never smite out our enemy until we understand not only how they see us,

21
00:02:21,600 --> 00:02:22,920
but how they see themselves.

22
00:02:23,660 --> 00:02:31,680
I think you'll find, sir, that there will come a time when black people wake up

23
00:02:31,680 --> 00:02:38,540
and become intellectually independent enough to think for themselves.

24
00:02:38,660 --> 00:02:43,220
As other humans are intellectually independent enough to think for themselves,

25
00:02:43,840 --> 00:02:46,540
then the black man will think like a black man.

26
00:02:46,540 --> 00:02:50,220
And he will feel for other black people.

27
00:02:50,940 --> 00:02:55,460
And this new thinking and feeling will cause black people to stick together.

